  "conversion_warnings": [
    "degree_type corrected BA -> BS per catalog (program is the B.S. in Artificial Intelligence, housed in the School of Business).",
    "Program is housed in the RIC School of Business; CSCI/DATA/CIS subjects supply the technical core, MATH the cognates, and BUSI 100 the business-orientation course (waivable via COLL 101/COLL 150/HONR 150/NURS 100 per catalog note).",
    "Catalog 'Total Credit Hours: 54' is the MAJOR total NET of an 8-credit overlap: a catalog note states 'Eight credit hours from BIOL 111; CHEM 103; MATH 212, MATH 240; or PHYS 101 may be counted toward the Natural Science and Mathematics categories of General Education.' Gross major credits as modeled = 62 (cognates 8 + science sequence 8 + core 18 + additional required 12 + 3 AI electives 12 + 1 data/analytics elective 4); 62 - 8 shared = 54 unique major credits.",
    "total_credits=120 set to the RIC institutional graduation minimum (>=120 earned credits, >=45 at RIC, >=15 in major with >=12 at 300/400-level, cumulative GPA >= 2.00); the program page lists only the 54-credit major.",
    "Credit model to 120 (counting the 8 shared science/math credits exactly once, inside the major blocks): major blocks 62 (gross) + General Education 32 (the 40-credit, 9-category RIC gen-ed reduced by the 8 credits already counted in the major) + free electives 26 = 120. RIC General Education is >=40 credits across 9 categories (3 Core: First Year Seminar, First Year Writing, + one of Math/Natural Science; and 6 Distribution incl. Arts, History/Philosophy, Literature/Language, Social & Behavioral Sciences, Connections).",
    "General Education and free electives modeled as wildcard '*:*' select pools (no individual gen-ed courses enumerated), per generation guidance for open distribution buckets.",
    "'ONE OF THE FOLLOWING TWO-COURSE SEQUENCES' (BIOL 111+112 / CHEM 103+104 / PHYS 101+102) modeled as type one_of with three options, each an 'all' 2-course pair.",
    "Prerequisites traced from the live 2024-2025 RIC course pages (sc_prereqs blocks). Placement/standing prerequisites that are not degree courses were modeled as null: 'Completed college mathematics milestone' / math-placement (CSCI 211, CSCI 342W's '45 credit hours', MATH 240, BIOL 111, CHEM 103, PHYS 101), and the MATH 120 / MATH 209 developmental placement chain (so MATH 212 prereq null, CSCI 209's '... and MATH 120' dropped).",
    "Non-existent alternative course codes in the 2024-2025 catalog were folded/dropped: 'CSCI 212' (pre-W equivalent) -> CSCI 212W; 'CSCI 221' (does not exist) dropped from CSCI 212W's prereq leaving CSCI 211; 'CIS 352' (does not exist) dropped from CIS 470/472 prereqs leaving CIS 252; 'CSCI 315' (does not exist) dropped from CSCI 423's prereq leaving CSCI 212W.",
    "Out-of-program prerequisite courses are fully defined so no reference dangles: CSCI 157, CSCI 102, CSCI 423, CIS 252, CIS 301, MATH 248, MATH 315, MATH 436. Their own placement-only prerequisites (MATH 120/177/300, CIS 252's '15 credits') were terminated at null. This corrects the skeletal source, which had 'pruned 21 dangling prerequisite reference(s)'.",
